<title>USA: U.S. May retail sales fell 0.1 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. May retail sales fell 0.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   May    Apr-(Prev)  May97/96</p>
<p> Retail Sales	   -0.1   -0.9  -0.3     3.0</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	-0.1   -0.5  -0.1     3.2</p>
<p> Auto Sales	     -0.2   -2.0  -0.9     2.6</p>
<p> Durable Goods	  -0.3   -1.2  -0.5     3.1</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods     Unch   -0.6  -0.3     3.0</p>
<p> Furniture Stores	0.6    0.8  -0.3     4.3</p>
<p> Building Materials   -0.6   -0.3  Unch     7.2</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  May     Apr-(Previous)    Mar--(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 210.30   210.52  212.24   212.40  212.97</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    159.56   159.66  160.38   160.50  160.61</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    50.74    50.86   51.86    51.90   52.36</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 85.75    86.00   87.09    87.08   87.50</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   124.55   124.52  125.15   125.32  125.47</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.65    11.58   11.43    11.49   11.46</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.96    12.02   12.02    12.06   12.02</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:   May    Apr-(Prev)  May97/96</p>
<p> General Merch.Stores  0.7   -1.0  -0.9     4.4</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.7   -1.2  -1.0     5.1</p>
<p> Food Stores	     0.2   -0.6  -0.5     2.9</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	  0.1   -0.5  -0.5     2.6</p>
<p> Gas Stations	   -0.7   -1.3  -0.1    -1.9</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	  0.8   -0.5  -0.6     0.4</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places     -1.0   -1.3   0.5     1.2</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     0.2   -0.6  -0.1     8.2</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  May     Apr-(Previous)</p>
<p>Mar----(Prev)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    27.29    27.11    27.23     27.39   27.49</p>
<p> Department Stores   21.45    21.30    21.42     21.55   21.63</p>
<p> Food Stores	   36.03    35.97    35.88     36.17   36.06</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.95    33.92    33.79     34.08   33.97</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  13.03    13.12    13.26     13.29   13.28</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.61     9.53     9.56	9.59    9.62</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    19.89    20.08    20.60     20.34   20.50</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    8.09     8.07     8.13	8.12    8.14</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected May retail sales to rise 0.4 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The May retail sales drop is the third consecutive monthly decline. The last time retail sales dropped three months in a row was during September to November 1981.</p>
<p>April's revised 0.9 percent drop in retail sales is the biggest decline since February 1995, when sales fell 1.6 percent.</p>
<p>The revised 2.0 percent drop in auto sales was the biggest decline in a year. Last April, auto sales were down 2.9 percent.</p>
